## Why This Is Asked
This question probes multi-tenant isolation, streaming ingestion, and end-to-end correctness in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant IAM and data isolation
- Pub/Sub topic naming strategy and Dataflow streaming
- BigQuery partitioning and clustering
- Schema validation and dead-letter handling
- Idempotent writes and testing with synthetic traffic

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Cloud Function: basic JSON validation scaffold
const Ajv = require('ajv');
const ajv = new Ajv();
const schema = { type: 'object', properties: { tenant_id: {type: 'string'}, events: {type: 'array'} }, required: ['tenant_id','events'] };
exports.validateLog = (event) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(event.data, 'base64').toString());
  const valid = ajv.validate(schema, data);
  if (!valid) throw new Error('Invalid schema');
  // publish to Pub/Sub per-tenant topic (omitted)
};
```

